        "original_id": "fd833032-0ba3-52f6-bb3a-93d2a14d3cd0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Fattest Man in Britain; Is There Nothing We Could Do?\n- People: Caroline Aherne; Jeff Pope; David Blair; Timothy Spall; Bobby Ball; Aisling Loftus; Barry Austin; Robert Harper; Tommy Cannon\n- Roles: Writer; Director; Actor; Comedian; Singer\n- Organizations: ITV; STV; UTV\n- Concepts: Cannon and Ball\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Harper, professionally known as Bobby Ball, was born on 28 January 1944 and is an English comedian, actor, and singer.\n- Bobby Ball is best known as one half of the double act Cannon and Ball with Tommy Cannon.\n- The Fattest Man in Britain is a comedy-drama written by Caroline Aherne and Jeff Pope and directed by David Blair.\n- The Fattest Man in Britain starred Timothy Spall, Bobby Ball, Aisling Loftus, and Barry Austin.\n- The Fattest Man in Britain aired on ITV, STV, and UTV on 20 December 2009.\n- Is There Nothing We Could Do? contains music inspired by the television film The Fattest Man in Britain.",
